WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.350
2018's Halloween pushes beyond the limits
of a normal slasher flick, particularly its

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:06.640
rather abrupt ending.

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:10.570
If you're itching to unravel the different
moving parts left in the wake of Michael Myers'

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:13.730
latest rampage, here's Halloween's ending
and aftermath explained.

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:17.620
Oh, and it should go without saying, but spoilers
for the entire film are ahead.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:22.730
We learn by the end of Halloween that Michael
Myers isn't the only source of darkness in

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:23.420
the film.

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:28.060
This time, the doctor who's fascinated by
him takes things to a truly dangerous level.

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:32.259
He reveals his true colors when he murders
Sheriff Frank Hawkins rather than let Michael

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:35.220
die, all in an effort to truly understand
the serial killer.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:38.980
Sartain's heel-turn seems to indicate that
the bus crash that kicked the movie's murder

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:41.520
spree off was almost certainly his doing.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:45.860
While we never actually see how that happened,
Sartain's obsession with Michael and the fact

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:49.850
that Myers was locked in the back of the bus,
while Sartain sat up front near the driver

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:53.781
sure makes it seem like the not-so-good doctor
was the reason the bus crashed and Michael

00:00:53.781 --> 00:00:54.400
went free.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:59.340
Karen Strode spends much of Halloween outwardly
fearful of and hostile toward her mother,

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:01.580
who she blames for her own dysfunctional life.

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:04.989
Then, in an instant, with her back against
the wall, Karen Strode remembers what her

00:01:04.989 --> 00:01:08.970
mother taught her, luring Michael Myers into
the basement stairway just long enough to

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:13.130
get off a wounding shot and begin the process
of trapping the monster once and for all.

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:16.740
It's a cathartic moment not just because it
proves that Laurie was right to be prepared

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:20.939
all along, but also because it allows Karen
to turn all that fear and distraction she's

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:24.200
been grappling with her whole life into a
moment of genuine power.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:28.759
Laurie carries most of the burden of the confrontation
with Michael, but all three Strode women change

00:01:28.759 --> 00:01:33.119
in the process, and Karen's change might end
up being the most powerful if she can learn

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:34.280
the right lessons from it.

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:38.840
In the final moments of the movie, we see
that Laurie's granddaughter Allyson has not

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:42.959
yet let go of Michael's knife, which, just
moments earlier, she used as a key weapon

00:01:42.959 --> 00:01:43.959
in fighting him.

00:01:43.959 --> 00:01:48.090
The way the knife hangs limp and bloody in
her hand seems like a very clear visual reference

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:51.899
to the way in which young Michael held his
first knife after his own first murder back

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:54.400
in 1963, when he was just a boy.

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:58.920
Is Allyson simply shell-shocked from the violence,
or is something deeper and darker at work

00:01:58.920 --> 00:01:59.420
here?

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:01.120
Perhaps we'll find out one day.

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:06.280
By the end of this film, Laurie Strode herself
has become a legend in contrast to that of

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:06.780
Michael's own.

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:11.000
She's built on the reputation she's established
as the paranoid old woman who lives out in

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.400
the woods, and has become something more.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.240
She's the Woman Who Killed The Boogeyman.

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:19.680
We don't get to see any of the aftermath of
that play out in this film, but it's a powerful

00:02:19.689 --> 00:02:23.659
narrative, and any number of journalists and
other public figures are bound to take an

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:28.000
interest in telling her story, and perhaps
setting Laurie on the road to true recovery.

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:33.120
Now it's time to discuss what will undoubtedly
be the most-debated, most important element

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:36.780
of Halloween's ending: Whether or not Michael
Myers is actually dead.

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:41.140
This film ignores all the previous sequels,
so we go into it with no real hint that Michael

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:42.780
is anything but a sadistic killer.

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:45.439
He's evil, but physically he's just a guy,
right?

00:02:45.439 --> 00:02:49.280
Well, that's a question a potential sequel
might need to explore, because while it's

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:53.090
clear that Laurie, Karen, and Allyson are
able to trap Michael in the basement and then

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:57.099
light the whole house on fire, it isn't clear
if that actually kills Michael.

00:02:57.099 --> 00:03:00.680
We see a few moments where he's surrounded
by flames, but the last thing we see happen

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:04.220
at Laurie's place is the fire beginning to
engulf the exterior of the house.

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:08.950
We do get one more shot of the basement as
the house burns…and he's not there.

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:13.001
We don't ever see a body, which leaves plenty
of wiggle room for Michael to escape, whether

00:03:13.001 --> 00:03:17.110
through supernatural means or just wriggling
through a gap in the floorboards because,

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:19.459
remember, Laurie shot through them at one
point.

00:03:19.459 --> 00:03:22.870
And of course, viewers who stayed through
the credits got to hear some creepy, ominous

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:24.640
breathing before leaving the theater.

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:28.560
Sure seems like a heavy hint that Michael
indeed found a way to survive...

